      "id": "xwdm0fw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Disease"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Diseases are broadly classified into Communicable (infectious) and Non-Communicable (non-infectious) diseases.",
        "Deficiency diseases occur due to a lack of specific vitamins, minerals, or essential nutrients in the diet over a long period.",
        "The immune system consists of innate immunity (present at birth) and acquired immunity (developed after exposure to pathogens).",
        "Vaccination works by introducing killed or weakened antigens to stimulate antibody production and build long-term memory.",
        "Preventive measures include maintaining hygiene, balanced nutrition, vector control, and timely immunization schedules."
      ],
      "id": "c1ns5xo"
    },
