    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Edward Jenner is known as the 'Father of Vaccination' for developing the smallpox vaccine in 1796.",
        "Key deficiency diseases frequently asked: Vitamin A (Night Blindness), Vitamin C (Scurvy), Vitamin D (Rickets), and Iodine (Goitre).",
        "Distinguish between Active Immunity (body produces own antibodies) and Passive Immunity (direct transfer of readymade antibodies)."
      ],
